  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "If you are experiencing irregular discharge and irritation, it is important to take steps to alleviate symptoms before seeking medical attention. Here are some steps you can take:\n\n1. Wash your genital area with mild soap and water. Avoid using harsh soaps or scented products.\n\n2. Avoid sexual intercourse until the symptoms have subsided.\n\n3. Avoid using tampons or other feminine hygiene products that may irritate the area.\n\n4. Wear loose-fitting, breathable clothing made of cotton.\n\n5. Avoid wearing tight underwear or pants that may cause friction.\n\n6. Avoid using douches or other products that may disrupt the natural balance of your vagina.\n\n7. Avoid using irritants such as alcohol or hot water.\n\n8. Avoid smoking or using tobacco products.\n\n9. Maintain a healthy diet and stay hydrated.\n\n10. Practice good hygiene by washing your hands before and after using the bathroom.\n\nIf your symptoms persist or worsen, it is important to seek medical attention.",
